# Single-Operator Mode (Boz)

**Precedence:** When this rule conflicts with team-oriented guidance in `anvil-stack.mdc`, `autonomous-development-lifecycle.mdc`, `anvil-task-system.mdc`, `project-creation.mdc`, `anvil-output-contract.mdc`, or mirrored copies in project `.cursor/rules/`, **this rule wins** for workflow and process. Do **not** edit auto-generated rule bodies to reflect solo mode — this companion file is the override.

**Context:** Boz is the sole operator. Default assumption is **one active Cursor session** unless he explicitly opens parallel agents or Cowork sessions. Team rules exist for historical multi-session incidents; they are guidance, not blockers, in solo mode.

---

## Session & coordination (relaxed)

| Team rule | Solo override |
|---|---|
| **Component ownership lease** (`cove-session-leases` KV) mandatory before editing hub-mcp, pulse, etc. | **Optional.** Acquire a lease only when Boz has **parallel sessions** open on the same component, or when he asks for coordination. Skip for normal single-session work. |
| **Branch-per-session** — never edit `main` directly | **Recommended, not mandatory.** Prefer `agent/<intent>` branches for non-trivial or deploy-bound work. Direct commits to `main` are acceptable for trivial fixes when Boz approves and CI will gate merge. |
| Multi-session divergence warnings | Assume **single session** unless told otherwise. Session-start triage (`git fetch`, `git status`, reconcile pending) stays **recommended** at session start — low cost, high value. |
| End-of-session sweep with lease/ticket delta lines | End-of-session: `git status --short`, commit/push or stash. **No lease reporting** unless a lease was actually held. |

---

## Git, PRs, and merge (solo)

| Team rule | Solo override |
|---|---|
| Never merge without explicit approval | Merge/self-merge is allowed when **Boz approves** (explicit "merge", "ship it", "go ahead", or standing automerge instruction for the task). No external reviewer required. |
| Draft PR default | PRs may be **ready for review** (non-draft) when Boz wants fast iteration. Draft is fine for WIP. |
| Required reviews complete (automerge gate) | **Not required** in solo repos. Boz is the reviewer. |
| Automerge eligible only with external review | **Automerge eligible** when ALL hold: Boz approved automerge or gave ship instruction; PR not draft (unless explicitly merging draft); **CI fully passing**; branch mergeable; no unresolved security findings; no pending migrations needing approval; no known production blockers. **External review is not a gate.** |
| Force push to `main`/`master` | **Still forbidden** unless Boz explicitly requests it. |

**Self-merge path:** push branch → open PR (optional for trivial) → wait for green CI → merge when Boz approves. Squash or merge commit per repo convention.

### Cloud agents & Cursor (solo)

| Team rule | Solo override |
|---|---|
| **Branch-per-session** (`agent/<intent>`) | Cloud agents use `cursor/<intent>-f909` per cloud task config; local solo work may use `agent/<intent>` or direct `main` for trivial fixes. |
| **Draft PR default** | Mark PR **ready for review** when Boz wants merge; draft only for WIP. |
| **PR update / label / merge via agent API** | **Not available** on built-in Cursor token (`updatePullRequest`). **Fix:** add `GH_TOKEN` PAT to Cursor Cloud Environment (see `docs/cursor-github-integration.md`). **Fallback:** git push only + [Cursor Agent Auto Ship](.github/workflows/cursor-agent-auto-ship.yml) or `/ship` comment. |
| **External review required** | Not required for eligible low-risk `cursor/**` PRs — auto-ship workflow approves + squash merges when CI green. Non-cursor branches: add label `automerge:low-risk`. |
| **Component ownership lease** | Skip unless parallel sessions on the same component. |

